  "goodToKnow": "Der Aberglaube (also der Aberglauben) is superstition. German superstitions include knocking on wood (auf Holz klopfen), saying toi, toi, toi before a performance, not wishing happy birthday early, and seeing a schwarze Katze from the left as bad luck. Lucky charms are der Schornsteinfeger (chimney sweep), das vierblättrige Kleeblatt and das Hufeisen. Abergläubisch means superstitious. It has no plural."
